Z||000000||AkursedX||03-28-2001||02:50 PM||||Ok, well I'm at the local super-market returning bottles, and on my way out, I was scoping out all the cars and my eyes fall onto an 88-92 Mustang LX 5.0.<P>First of all, this car was pretty beat, and it still had one of those big fiberglass hoods, and it had 13inch lowrider wire rims on it. Just another case bad taste as far as I'm concerned.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>But.........I look along the bottom of the doors, and there are Chrome step bars along each side  (Like the ones you would see on something like a Dodge Ram)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  They were probably like 4 inch rails and they extended from wheel-well to wheel-well.<P>This has to be one of the stupidest things I have ever seen!  First of all, it was just plain UGLY.  And second of all, unless the driver was 2 feet tall, there was absolutley no use for them!!   ||||reg||13
